cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "reader-ergonomics-topic (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  One template for a unit of writing whose parts can be units of the same
  template, so that any body of information is written as a tree that reads
  the same way at every depth. It builds on reader-ergonomics. It holds the
  template, a check a program runs on it at any depth, and three reviews of
  the evidence; no reader study has tested it yet.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/reader-ergonomics-topic"
license:
